---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us — Shangri-La Yunnan Travel Guide"
  description="Shangri-La Guide: first-hand travel tips for Shangri-La Yunnan. Attractions, transport, food, and culture - written by a Yunnan-based travel team."
>
  <!-- Person Schema -->
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Shangri-La Guide Team",
    "description": "A small team of travel writers and photographers based in Yunnan, China. Collectively spent over 200 days traveling across northwest Yunnan. All content verified first-hand.",
    "knowsAbout": ["Shangri-La Travel", "Yunnan Tourism", "Tibetan Buddhist Culture", "High-Altitude Trekking", "China Travel Planning"],
    "nationality": { "@type": "Country", "name": "China" },
    "affiliation": {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Shangri-La Guide",
      "url": "https://shangri-la-yunnan.com"
    }
  }
  </script>
  <main class="pt-16">
    <div class="bg-slate-50 border-b border-slate-100">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-emerald-600">About</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">About Shangri-La Guide</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">Your trusted resource for planning the perfect trip to one of China's most extraordinary destinations.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Our Story</h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Shangri-La Guide was born from a simple frustration: planning a trip to Shangri-La was harder than it should be. Information was scattered across dozens of forums, outdated blog posts, and conflicting travel agency pages. There was no single, reliable source that covered everything &mdash; from altitude sickness to yak butter tea, from monastery chanting schedules to minivan departure times.</p>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">We set out to fix that. Shangri-La Guide is the result of multiple trips to Diqing Tibetan Autonomous Prefecture, conversations with local Tibetan families, monastery visits at dawn, and a lot of time spent on bumpy mountain roads. Every piece of information on this site has been verified first-hand.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 mt-10">Who We Are</h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Shangri-La Guide is maintained by a small team of travel writers and photographers based in Yunnan. We have collectively spent over <strong>200 days</strong> traveling across northwest Yunnan &mdash; from the cobblestone lanes of Dukezong Old Town to the high-altitude passes of Meili Snow Mountain. We speak Mandarin, and some of us speak basic Tibetan.</p>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">We are not affiliated with any hotel, tour company, or government tourism bureau. Our recommendations are based on experience, not commissions. When we say a guesthouse has the best yak hotpot in town, it is because we have eaten there multiple times and compared it to others.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 mt-10">Our Commitment</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
          <li><strong>First-hand information.</strong> Every ticket price, bus schedule, and opening hour on this site has been checked in person. We update prices at least twice a year.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest recommendations.</strong> We do not accept payment for positive reviews. If we recommend a place, it is because we genuinely believe it is worth your time and money.</li>
          <li><strong>Respect for local culture.</strong> We write about Tibetan Buddhist traditions with care and accuracy. Our cultural guides are reviewed by local Tibetan consultants.</li>
          <li><strong>Accessibility.</strong> Shangri-La travel information should be available in English. Many official local resources are Chinese-only, leaving international travelers with second-hand information. We bridge that gap.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 mt-10">Last Updated</h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">This guide was last updated in <strong>August 2026</strong>. We review all prices, transport schedules, and practical information every 6 months. Weather data is based on historical averages from the Diqing meteorological station.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 mt-10">Contact</h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">For corrections, suggestions, or media inquiries, email us at <a href="mailto:hello@shangri-la-yunnan.com" class="text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-700 underline">hello@shangri-la-yunnan.com</a>. We read every message and appreciate your help in keeping this guide accurate and useful.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">&copy; 2024&ndash;2026 Shangri-La Guide.</p>
      <a href="/" class="text-sm text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors font-medium">Back to Home</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>